From: aarchbio <noreply@aarch.bio>
Subject: [PATCH] launcher: accept Linux aarch64

The launcher accepts uname -m "arm64" (macOS) but not "aarch64", which is what
Linux reports on 64-bit ARM, so rtg refuses to start on Graviton and other
aarch64 Linux hosts. The Java code itself runs fine there.

---
--- a/rtg
+++ b/rtg
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
     # If you comment this check out you are on your own :-)
     echo "Sorry, only Linux and MacOS are supported."
     exit 1
-elif [[ "$(uname -m)" != "x86_64" ]] && [[ "$(uname -m)" != "arm64" ]]; then
+elif [[ "$(uname -m)" != "x86_64" ]] && [[ "$(uname -m)" != "arm64" ]] && [[ "$(uname -m)" != "aarch64" ]]; then
     # If you comment this check out you are on your own :-)
     echo "Sorry, you must be running a 64bit operating system."
     exit 1
